<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skouriotissa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Skouriotissa is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> mine in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, near the village of Katydata, and one of the oldest mining sites in the world still exploited. Its huge ancient slag heaps show copper working from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> through Roman times, when it supplied the nearby city of Soloi. Mining resumed there in the 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/skouriotissa.jpg" alt="Skouriotissa" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dr.Tzeferis Peter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skouriotissa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
